# Patch description:
# 
# 1. BUILD: Adds textual_hdrs for composing_executor.cc (so
#    ElasticComposingExecutor can #include it for internal types like
#    ExecutorValue, UnplacedInner, etc.) and makes the following targets
#    publicly visible (needed by elastic_composing_executor and its tests):
#    composing_executor, computations, executor_service,
#    federated_intrinsics, value_validation.
# 2. composing_executor.cc:
#    - Adds ClientsData/CentralClients types so that the elastic executor
#      can store per-client data centrally rather than distributing it to
#      children at creation time, enabling dynamic redistribution on failure.
#    - Makes overridable methods virtual and protected so that
#      ElasticComposingExecutor can override federated intrinsic handling.
#    - Makes data members protected for subclass access.
#    - Gates factory function with #ifndef to avoid ODR violations when the
#      .cc file is textually included.
# 3. federating_executor.cc: MAP loop uses data.clients()->size() instead
#    of num_clients_ to support variable client counts.
# 4. value_validation.cc: Removes strict client count check so that
#    ElasticComposingExecutor can pass batches with fewer clients than
#    the configured total.
# 5. Python BUILD: Makes executor_bindings and cpp_to_python_executor
#    targets publicly visible.
